---
import {
  Bug,
  ExternalLink,
  Monitor,
  Shield,
  Smartphone,
} from "@lucide/astro";
import { DESKTOP_REPO, DISCORD_INVITE_URL, REPO } from "../../../config/site";
---

<section
  id="report-bugs"
  class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface p-7 md:p-10"
>
  <div
    class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-vega-accent"
  >
    <Bug class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
    Reporting Bugs
  </div>

  <h1
    class="mt-4 font-headline text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3.1rem)] font-black tracking-tight text-white"
  >
    Report Errors with App Logs
  </h1>

  <p class="mt-3 max-w-[72ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">
    Attaching a clean app log is the fastest way to get playback errors,
    crashes, or casting issues fixed. Clear older entries, enable detailed
    logging, reproduce the problem once, and export the log file right away.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 space-y-5">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <Smartphone class="h-5 w-5 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h2 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">
          1. Capture &amp; Export Logs on Android (Mobile)
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ol
        class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>
          Open <strong class="text-white"
            >Settings &gt; About &amp; updates</strong
          > (labeled <strong class="text-white">About Vega</strong> on Google Play
          Store builds) and scroll down to <strong class="text-white"
            >Troubleshooting</strong
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tap <strong class="text-white">Clear logs</strong> first so unrelated history
          from earlier sessions is removed before you capture your bug.
        </li>
        <li>
          Turn on <strong class="text-white">Detailed logging</strong>. This
          records debug-level events and increases the rolling log limit from
          ~500 KB to ~2 MB. It automatically turns itself off after 24 hours.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Recreate the error:</strong> Go back to the
          screen where the problem happens and repeat the exact steps (open the title,
          start playback, trigger a cast/download, or reproduce the crash).
        </li>
        <li>
          Return immediately to <strong class="text-white"
            >Settings &gt; About &amp; updates</strong
          > (or <strong class="text-white">About Vega</strong>) &gt; <strong
            class="text-white">Troubleshooting</strong
          > and tap <strong class="text-white">Export logs</strong> to save or share
          the log file.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-vega-muted"
            >(Optional) Toggle <strong class="text-white"
              >Detailed logging</strong
            > back off once you finish, or let it expire automatically after 24 hours.</span
          >
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-3.5">
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">
          <strong class="text-white">Android TV note:</strong> The in-app Troubleshooting
          log controls are currently shown on phones and tablets, not Android TV.
          For TV-only bugs, describe your TV model, Android TV version, and exact
          reproduction steps when opening an issue.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <Monitor class="h-5 w-5 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h2 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">
          2. Capture &amp; Export Logs on Desktop
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ol
        class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>
          Open <strong class="text-white">Settings</strong> and scroll to the
          <strong class="text-white">About</strong> section.
        </li>
        <li>
          Turn on <strong class="text-white">Detailed Logging</strong>. This expands
          the rolling log limit from ~500 KB to ~4 MB and automatically turns off
          after 24 hours.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Recreate the error</strong> right away. Fresh
          events are appended with UTC timestamps at the bottom of the file, and
          the export automatically prepends OS, WebView, FFmpeg, and (on Linux) display
          session and GStreamer details.
        </li>
        <li>
          Return to <strong class="text-white">Settings &gt; About</strong>,
          click <strong class="text-white">Export</strong> next to <strong
            class="text-white">Export Logs</strong
          >, and save the <code
            class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >vega-logs-&lt;timestamp&gt;.txt</code
          > file.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <Shield class="h-5 w-5 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h2 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">
          3. What Logs Contain &amp; Automatic Privacy Filtering
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ul
        class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Normal vs. detailed logging:</strong> Normal
          mode keeps <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >info</code
          >, <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >warn</code
          >, <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >error</code
          >, and fatal crashes/panics. Turning on detailed logging adds debug
          and verbose messages from both the UI and native/Rust layers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Sanitized before writing:</strong> Vega strips
          URL query parameters (<code
            class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >https://example.com/path?…</code
          >) and masks sensitive values (<code
            class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white">cookie</code
          >, <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >set-cookie</code
          >, <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >authorization</code
          >, <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >x-api-key</code
          >, <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >token</code
          >, <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >api_key</code
          >, and <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white"
            >password</code
          > on Desktop) with <code
            class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white">&lt;hidden&gt;</code
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Review before sharing:</strong> Because the
          export is plain text, you can open it in any text editor to inspect or
          trim anything before uploading it.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-vega-accent/30 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-white">
        4. What to Include in Your Bug Report
      </h2>
      <ul
        class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>
          Attach the exported <code
            class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white">.txt</code
          > log file directly instead of pasting screenshots of text.
        </li>
        <li>
          State your device model, OS version, Vega version, update channel
          (Stable or Beta), and whether you use the GitHub or Store build.
        </li>
        <li>
          Write numbered steps to reproduce the issue, what you expected to
          happen, and what happened instead (add screenshots or a short video for
          UI/layout bugs).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-vega-accent px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-[#240900] transition hover:-translate-y-0.5"
          href={`${REPO.url}/issues`}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          <ExternalLink class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
          Report Android/TV Issue
        </a>
        <a
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-white transition hover:bg-white/12"
          href={`${DESKTOP_REPO.url}/issues`}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          <ExternalLink class="h-4 w-4 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          Report Desktop Issue
        </a>
        <a
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-white transition hover:bg-white/12"
          href={DISCORD_INVITE_URL}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          <ExternalLink class="h-4 w-4 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          Share on Discord
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
